{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Golden Eyes
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = Any [[Kaelensia]]
}}
''The golden, beast-like eyes of the Kaelensia reduce the effectiveness of Blindness by SAN*2 (at 25 SAN, this means no Hit penalty is applied, even if you have the status).''
{{KaelensiaLL}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Flight
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Corbie]]
}}
''This unit, having wings, is capable of flight. While Airborne, this unit will hover when using Movement, allowing them to avoid field hazards and traps on the ground.''
{{Corbie}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Aerial Attacker
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Corbie]]
}}
''Best suited to attacking from the air. In battle, while you are Airborne, you gain +10 Hit, and a bonus to Power equal to 1 + 30% of your Scaled SAN.''
{{Corbie}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Flaming Feathers
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Phenex]]
}}
''The wings of the Phenex protect from certain elements, namely Fire and Light, granting a 15% Elemental Resistance to those elements. However, the same can not be said of Ice and Darkness damage, and the Phenex takes 15% increased damage from those elements. Furthermore, a limited ability to hover lets them use Movement while Airborne.''
{{Phenex}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = From the Ashes
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Phenex]]
}}
''The power of the Phenex clan was shown once by Heldonis, and his people are not much different. When the Phenex is reduced to 0 HP, if they have at least 1 FP, half of that FP is consumed and the Phenex restores that much HP immediately (min. 1 HP; the FP consumption is reduced by your Scaled SAN%, but the HP restored is not). This effect can only trigger once per 10 Rounds, reduced by 10% of your Scaled SAN.''
{{Phenex}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Heron Physique
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Heron]]
}}
''Herons are greatly in-tune with aural forces, and are more than resilient to them, granting +15% Sound Resistance. Their wings are unused to harsh gales, however, giving them a 15% Wind Weakness.''
{{Heron}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Fleetfoot
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Felidae]], [[Grimalkin]]
}}
''Being the fast creatures that they are, this unit gains +1 Move.''
{{Felidae}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Dark Claws
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Shaitan]]
}}
''Powerful black carapace protects and increases the force of the Shaitan's attacks. They gain +6 (-1 per 10 Scaled SAN) damage to all attacks made with non-ranged weaponry.''


{{Shaitan}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Future Vision
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Oracle]]
}}
''An Oracle's vision of far-off places is always clouded with visions of the future, decreasing their Hit and Evade by 10% against any enemy beyond 1 Range. However, the Oracle also sees the future movements of enemies within 1 Range, increasing their Hit and Evade versus them by 10%. All bonuses and penalties are reduced by 1 per 10 Scaled SAN.''


{{Corrupted}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Healer's Legacy
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Elf]]
}}
''When healing an ally or themself with a healing spell or staff battle item, the base Power of that spell is increased by your Scaled SAN. Additionally, when crafting items using the Alchemy skill, they gain +1 bonus Crafting EXP.''
{{Elf}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Arcane Order
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Lich]]
}}
''The stability that defines the ritual that creates a Lich. At high amounts of Focus, this pact is at its strongest, nullifying the chance of divine intervention. When at 60% (-1% per 1 Scaled SAN) FP or higher, the Lich cannot critically, nor can they be critically hit.''
{{Lich}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Dissipate
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Lich]]
}}
''Upon destruction of the physical body of the Lich, the arcane energy that actually comprises the Lich returns to the phylactery. Liches will often enchant their belongings to return along with it, greatly reducing the chance that items will be dropped upon defeat in battle.''
{{Lich}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Golden Blood
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Glykin]]
}}
''A divine blood that fills the Glykin. They gain immunity to Poison and regenerate 1 (+1 per 2 Scaled SAN) HP every round in combat (max: 10). Any Vampire that tries to Feed on the Glykin will take Light damage. There is also a Faith% chance that any negative status applied to them that lasts 3 rounds or more will be reduced by 1 round.''


{{Glykin}}
{{SerpentkindLL}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Fire Wing
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Hyattr]]
}}
''The scaled dragon wings of the Hyattr protect them from Fire, which is their signature element anyway, increasing their Fire Resistance by 15%. However, those same wings are vulnerable to the winds they fly on, increasing their Wind weakness by 15%.''


{{Hyattr}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Artifical Body
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Mechanation]]
}}
''As a Mechanation's form is very different from a natural creature's, they are less vulnerable to Fire and Ice damage, reducing each by 15%. However, they also suffer a 25% weakness to Electricity as a result.''


{{Mechanation}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Forest Family
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Doriad]]
}}
''As beings born from plants, the Doriad doesn't particular mind things like Water and Earth damage, reducing it by 15%. The same cannot be said for Fire and Darkness, which they take 15% more damage from.''
{{Doriad}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Burden Soul
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Dullahan]]
}}
''The strength of the Dullahan is spiritual in nature, resulting in a body that is less affected by the weight of its collective. Increases your Battle Weight limit by 100, and your maximum carrying capacity by 30. Furthermore, the Interference status, which normally prevents HP and FP recovery, is only half as effective on Dullahans, meaning they still recover 50% of the original total. This resistance is increased by your Scaled SAN.''
{{Dullahan}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Homunculi Physique
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = All [[Homunculi]]
}}
''An artificially created lifeform. Received healing reduced by 15%. HP per point of VIT reduced by 0.5. FP per point of WIL increased by 1.''
{{HomunculiLL}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Drop of Nairyf
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Salamandra]]
}}
''Created from the divine energy of the dead elemental Nairyf. +15% Fire Resistance, -15% Cold Resistance. Immunity to Burn status.''
{{Salamandra}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Amalgama Mutation
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Amalgama]]
}}
''The unique nature of the Amalgama will gradually cause their body to 'mutate', giving them new abilities and weaknesses. While the body may not be visibly changed, the Amalgama will know the difference. Grants up to 11 random Amalgama skills, one every 5 character levels. (While the skills you gain are random, you will always gain a certain amount of a specific category, IE Attack, etc.)''
{{Amalgama Mutations}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname         = Artificial Body
 | sourcetext    = [[Mechanation]]
}}

''As a Mechanation's form is very different from a natural creature's, they are less vulnerable to Fire and Ice damage, reducing each by 15%. However, they also suffer a 25% weakness to Electricity as a result.''
{{Mechanation}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Graceless Destruction
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Oni]]
}}
''The only thing scarier than an Oni is a drunk Oni. While they are Clumsy, the Oni gains +5% Phys and Mag Defense, and deal +10% Critical Damage with melee weapons.''
{{Oni}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname         = Blood Binding
 | sourcetext    = [[Karakuri]]
}}

''Karakuri are created through blood ritual, one step of which involves binding a Youkai to its artificial body, creating a state similar to a permanent Install. As a result, Karakuri are always treated as youkai for effects that care about such a designation.''

''Karakuri who are summoners can still make use of Install normally. The type of youkai bound to the Karakuri can also be selected via a free Blood Binding trait, which will alter the Karakuri's base stats and elemental resistances.''
{{Karakuri}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Profession
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = Any [[Human]]
}}
''Humans commonly spend long times studying and preparing for a specific type of job. Thus, when buying a 'History' trait, it does not cost a Trait Point.''


{{Human}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Quick to Master
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = Any [[Human]]
}}
''Humans live in a world where they must constantly adapt to situations and circumstances they find themselves in, which makes them more versatile than other races. They gain +2 class skill points for every class. Additionally, their skill pool size is increased by 2, letting them equip more skills at once.''


{{Human}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Instinct (Lupine)
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Lupine]]
}}
''Lupines do not go down without a fight. In battle, while at 50% HP or less, they gain a bonus to STR, WIL, DEF, and RES equal to 1 + 10% of your Scaled SAN. At 25% HP or less, the bonus is doubled.''
{{Lupine}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Stay Afloat
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = Corbie
}}
''Toggle skill. While toggled on, all skills you use will be treated as if they were Airborne Compatible, meaning they won't end your Airborne status.''
{{Corbie}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Instinct (Felidae)
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Felidae]], [[Grimalkin]]
}}
''The Felidae are fast and when they feel like they're in danger, they get faster. In battle, while at 50% HP or less, they gain a bonus to SKI, CEL, LUC, and GUI equal to 1 + 10% of your Scaled SAN. At 25% HP or less, the bonus is doubled.''
{{Felidae}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Leporidae Physique
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Leporidae]]
}}
''More adept at using the ground to their advantage, or simply more capable of avoiding its dangers, the Leporidae is harder to hurt with Earth damage, giving them a 15% resistance to it. Their ears are incredibly powerful, but also somewhat sensitive, and so they take Sound damage harder than others, giving them a 15% weakness to it. Mumbling is also less effective against them.''
{{Leporidae}}
{{KaelensiaLL}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Instinct (Leporidae)
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Leporidae]]
}}
''Leporidae do not like being put into a corner, and when pushed, their keen senses come out in full force. When at 50% HP or less, the effect of Rabbit Foot increases by 50%. At 25% HP or less, when the Leporidae is targeted by a basic attack (or skill that uses a basic attack), before the attack happens, they turn to face the attacker.''
{{Leporidae}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Rabbit Foot
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Leporidae]]
}}
''Known for their strong legs, the Leporidae are certainly capable of delivering a painful kick. Lesser known is their natural affinity with weather magic, such as lightning, which is displayed better by wild monster hares. After using Rabbit Leap, the first Kick skill or Nature domain spell used this round gains bonus damage equal to (distance moved) + 50% of your Scaled SAN.''
{{Leporidae}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Scurry
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Muridae]]
}}
''Muridae are quick critters who are used to having to run from Felidae. When not wearing Heavy Armor, they gain +1 Move, and a bonus to their flee chance equal to Scaled SAN/2.''
{{Muridae}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Ratsense
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Muridae]]
}}
''Muridae hear things better in some situations than others. When trying to pick a lock, they gain +10% to the success rate. However, they are naturally oblivious of traps, giving them a -5% chance to detect them.''
{{Muridae}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Mind Scorch
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Shaitan]]
}}
''Their psyche assaulted by things far more terrifying than most, the Shaitan is immune to Fear (if below 30 SAN), Hesitation (if below 20 SAN), and Charm (if below 10 SAN).''


{{Shaitan}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Illusion Wing
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Papilion]]
}}
''Entities that thrive around deception like the Papilion are often compatible with elements that support illusions, such as the Wind, granting them 30% Resistance to it. However, the Earth element tells no lies, making Papilion 30% weak to it. Both effects are reduced by your Scaled SAN, to a minimum of 0.''


{{Papilion}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Theno Physique
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Theno]]
}}
''The unique physique offered by the Theno from spending all their time swimming and singing grants them +15% Water and Sound Resistance, but for the same reasons, gives them a 15% Acid and Lightning Weakness.''


{{Theno}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Voice of the Depths
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Theno]]
}}
''The voice of the Theno is powerful, magically so. You gain +25% Status Resistance versus Silence effects. In addition, your base Sound ATK is equal to your character level, but it does not increase from stat points.''


{{Theno}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Lost Sea
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Theno]]
}}
''When you live in the sea, there's not much to fear in the shallows. While your base SAN is 15 or less, you ignore the effects of Dark Water. In addition, Soaked status grants you +15 Evade.''

{{Theno}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Spotless
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Elf]]
}}
''Having built up no tolerance for the dark magic in the outside world, Elves suffer 25% more Dark damage. However, they have a natural resistance against Water damage, reducing damage they take from it by 25%.''
{{Elf}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Spotted
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Wild Elf]]
}}
''Wild Elves typically have slightly darker blotches of skin which resemble spots. The attunement with nature they provide increases Earth Resistance by 15%, but lowers Ice Resistance by 15%.''
{{Wild Elf}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Reaper Physique
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Reaper]], [[Apertaurus]]
}}
''Being used to the cold air inside of Lazarus, the Reaper race is more resistant to Ice damage, gaining 15% resistance to it. However, the still air inside of it has made them weaker to the power of Wind, gaining a 15% weakness to it.''
{{Reaper}}
{{Apertaurus}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Soul Guide
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Reaper]], [[Apertaurus]]
}}
''Reapers are agents of Lazarus with a duty to help guide the souls of the lost to it. As such, they are particularly skilled at dealing with those of the Possessed race, dealing +10% damage to them. They are also excellent exorcists, gaining a variety of bonuses; it costs them 50% less stamina to exorcise spirits, and upon successfully doing so, they gain a status effect that increases post-battle HP/FP regen by 10% for 10 rounds, with the duration stacking up to 100 rounds.''
{{Reaper}}
{{Apertaurus}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Macabre Culture
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Reaper]], [[Apertaurus]]
}}
''Reapers often wear bones over their clothes as decorations, and the rattling of them is something that serves as an easy indicator of their presence. When wearing equipment of Remains-type material (IE, Dragon Remains), the Reaper gains 2 Elemental ATK from that material, based on what left the remains behind.''
{{Reaper}}
{{Apertaurus}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Magia Detremus
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Lich]]
}}
''As they are beings mostly comprised of arcane energy, the vessel of the Lich has an almost limitless supply of Focus to draw upon, although it is limited still by time. Increases your maximum FP by 50% (after all modifications), but your maximum HP is reduced by 30% (after all modifications), due to the fragility of the vessel. Both the FP bonus and the HP penalty are increased/reduced respectively by 1% per 2 Scaled SAN.''
{{Lich}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Venom Drive
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Wyverntouched]]
}}
''Much like their ancestors, Wyverntouched are empowered by poison that flows in their body. When a Wyverntouched is under the effect of a Poison status, they gain +X STR (where X is equal to half the Poison's level) and recover 5 FP every round. Often, Wyverns would bite themselves, injecting their own venom into their blood to increase their power. In addition, Wyverntouched gain Poison Resistance equal to (Scaled SAN*2)%.''


{{Wyverntouched}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Snakescale
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Naga]]
}}
''Needless to say, the naga is half snake. This gives them several benefits common to the serpent races. Increases Slash resistance by 1% per 5 Scaled SAN, and increases Poison resistance by your Scaled SAN.''
{{Naga}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Mechanical Strength
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Mechanation]]
}}
''Unlike many mortal races, the Mechanation is not used to strain and exhaustion in the same way. They gain +20 to their maximum encumbrance. They also gain +1 maximum Physical and Mental Stamina every 2 character levels.''
{{Mechanation}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname         = Threaded Needle
 | sourcetext    = [[Karakuri]]
}}

''A level of mechanical precision afforded to the Karakuri through its string-guided movements. They passively gain +3% Parry Activation Rate, +3% Critical, and -1 Farshot Penalty. Additionally, this method of internal control makes them slightly more resilient to being Slowed, Frozen, or Immobilized, gaining +5% Status Resist versus those effects.''

''Through the use of traits, the Karakuri can also make use of its strings to perform unique feats. These effects will often 'exhaust the Karakuri's strings' for a certain period of time, during which skills and effects that would also exhaust the Karakuri's strings will not be able to be used. (In other words, a shared cooldown for these effects.)''
{{Karakuri}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]

{{Passivebox
 | sname        = Wyvern Assimilation
 | stype        = Racial
 | spec1        = '''Race'''
 | spec1text    = [[Salamandra]]
}}
''Infused with the blood of a wyvern. +30% status resistance versus Poison.''
{{Salamandra}}
[[Category:Skills]]
[[Category:Racial skills]]
